# StackRox UI Standards

## Component Library

- Use `@patternfly/react-core`, `@patternfly/react-table`, `@patternfly/react-icons`, and `@patternfly/react-charts` for all UI elements.
- Check `Components/PatternFly/` for project-specific PF wrappers (e.g. `LoadingSection`, `ConfirmationModal`, `ErrorBoundary`, `IconText`) before importing PF directly.
- Never introduce a third-party UI component when PatternFly already provides the equivalent.

## Component Patterns

- Functional components only — no class components.
- All props must have explicit TypeScript interfaces or type aliases. No `any` props.
- Colocate related files: component, types, utils, and test in the same directory.

## Styling

- Use PatternFly utility classes (`pf-v6-u-*`) for spacing, alignment, and layout.
- Do not write custom CSS unless PatternFly utility classes cannot achieve the layout. If custom CSS is needed, use a colocated `.css` file — not inline styles or styled-components.
- Never override PatternFly design tokens or CSS variables.

## Imports

- Use the path aliases from `tsconfig.json` (e.g. `Components/`, `Containers/`, `hooks/`, `services/`, `utils/`). Never use relative paths that climb above `src/`.
- Import PatternFly components from their top-level packages, not deep subpaths.

```typescript
// Correct
import { Button, Alert } from '@patternfly/react-core';
import { Table, Thead, Tr, Th, Td, Tbody } from '@patternfly/react-table';

// Wrong
import Button from '@patternfly/react-core/dist/esm/components/Button';
```
